{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561612-vtm-mtas-crossover-if-tremere-didn\u2019t-choose-vampirism","id":1561612,"title":"[VtM & MtAs crossover] If Tremere didn\u2019t choose vampirism?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-07-11T12:10:32-07:00","id":1561612,"title":"[VtM & MtAs crossover] If Tremere didn\u2019t choose vampirism?","content":"So I guess he would seek other immortality methods, like a variant of Lichdom, or even Infernalism like Nephadus. (Very likely, we all know his personality) Maybe he will outlive other Order\u2019s founders, but live until now is also a problem<br /> <br /> More importantly, how his House will influence Vampire/Mage forces? I don\u2019t know much about their history, I think the found of Camarilla and Technocracy will be influenced greatly? (Clan Tremere is a significant power behind Camarilla, and one of his apprentice Grimgroth made the Mistbridge fall and pushed the found of Technocracy greatly)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T13:06:50-07:00","id":1561613,"title":"","content":"The majority of the impact would be on the Mage side of things since it would rewrite a huge amount of Hermetic history.<br /> <br /> How much this would have changed VtM depends a lot on edition. In early VtM, the Tremere had a much stronger hold on blood magic. This made them vital to the pre-Camarilla and early Camarilla enough to justify overlooking the way they became vampires and how they created their gargoyles. In Revised and later... that role is reduced significantly. With the later takes on VtM where blood magic is more accessible, the Camarilla doesn't need the Tremere as much to have made it out on the other side of the late Medieval period in Europe. The biggest impact would probably be the geographic distribution of power:<br /> <br /> 1) The Sabbat would have likely been able to hold on to more of Europe as Abyssal mystics and Kolduns could have more impact without the sudden influx of sorcerers on the Cam's side of things<br /> 2) The Ashirra would probably remain more Banu Hakim controlled and possibly the outcome of their Schism would have gone differently, but they'd be in a stronger place to have a tense alliance with the Camarilla to keep the Sabbat on Setites at bay<br /> 3) The fight to colonize the Americas would have likely been much more competitive and fractured. Instead of the Sabbat largely getting their first and the Camarilla having to push in later","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-12T06:22:44-07:00","id":1561626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561612-vtm-mtas-crossover-if-tremere-didn\u2019t-choose-vampirism#post1561612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I guess he would seek other immortality methods, like a variant of Lichdom, or even Infernalism like Nephadus. (Very likely, we all know his personality) Maybe he will outlive other Order\u2019s founders, but live until now is also a problem<br /> <br /> More importantly, how his House will influence Vampire/Mage forces? I don\u2019t know much about their history, I think the found of Camarilla and Technocracy will be influenced greatly? (Clan Tremere is a significant power behind Camarilla, and one of his apprentice Grimgroth made the Mistbridge fall and pushed the found of Technocracy greatly)</div> </div> </div> </div>We do know his personality, and it suggests no infernalism. He, Goratrix, and the rest of House Tremere didn't like diabolism for a simple reason - if a demon is powerful enough to be worth summoning, it can't be controlled, and if it can be controlled, it isn't powerful enough to be worth it. He'd probably pursue lichdom or another Spell of Life variant. <br /> <br /> His remaining loyal to the Order of Hermes means not only that they don't have to deal with Grimgoth's betrayal, but also that they don't have to split resources between fighting the OoR and the Tremere, and that the Hermetics largely remain ignorant of the Camarilla, and likely don't have as big of a grudge against vampires. He or one of his House might eventually rise to political power within the Council of Nine, possibly even taking the role of Porthos in the main timeline. The OoR also might not win Mistridge, or at least have a much harder fight. If the OoR doesn't get Mistridge, then the Law of Shade likely doesn't exist, and Tradition magi operate openly, resulting in a radically different Consensus. <br /> <br /> As for the vampire history, the Banu Haqim don't get hit with the Tremere curse and continue being diablerists. This means that the Via Sanguinis mostly stays in its traditional form. This also means that when Ur-Shulgi wakes up, he doesn't have as much leverage, and in fact, may himself be on the menu. <br /> <br /> There are two realistic possibilities here - either the Banu Haqim join the Camarilla to fill the void in the timeline left by the Tremere, or the Sabbat fights the Camarilla on more equal ground as Koldunic sorcerers and Abyssal mystics beat them back (as Heavy Arms said). But then again, the Sabbat also loses troops; for example, the Salubri Warriors never join the Sabbat, since they're mostly there because the majority of Tremere are in the Camarilla. In fact, the Salubri in general are spared from the purges, and Saulot either never gets diablerized, or has to find another blood sorcerer to carry out his grand plan (possibly Ur-Shulgi). The Salubri likely become one of the pillars of the Camarilla, and make the Camarilla altogether a morally better group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-12T13:31:26-07:00","id":1561636,"title":"","content":"I actually think the bigger change would be VtM.<br /> <br /> Tremere would be OoH. Being he would be &quot;loyal&quot;, though, is a bit of a stretch.<br /> <br /> Overall I don't think they'd be invested enough to play a changing role in the events of Mage.<br /> <br /> Likely their efforts at immortality would have been limited but similar to others. The more they actually managed to achieve it, the less of a part they would have played in the events of Mage as they'd be more focused on their own affairs.<br /> <br /> Vampires would lack a big mover and shaker, not because Tremere were as powerful as they sold themselves, but because their desperation made them forcefully disruptive in the original timeline.<br /> <br /> Without them the Salubri would be a somewhat stronger presence. Mystics from other clans would have remained open and relevant, even growing stronger. We could have a variety of types of sorcery in the employ of various lords, possibly giving the Setites a place in &quot;polite&quot; vampiric society, attracting more Tzimisce Koldun defectors, even being possible a revival and strengthening of Ventrue sorcery.<br /> <br /> Given how much the Baali curse was a problem for the Banu Haqim, not a blessing, I don't think they'd change their trajectory so much. It would begin with a longer conflict, but peace would be brokered simply because it was unsustainable. And they were precisely the one sorcery tradition among the undead with the greater upper hand over the Sabbat, so they'd be sought after.<br /> <br /> Being diablerists would weight against them, but not enough to stop both their presence in the Camarilla and the formation of the Ashirra. I'd say their influence in the Ashirra would be smaller rather than greater, though, because they wouldn't be seen as sufficiently trustworthy.<br /> <br /> Details beyond those would depend a lot on the changed events, but finding a way to reverse the Baali Curse would be a possibility with many other sorcerous &quot;allies&quot; around and no other curse to fight. The Camarilla could also have devoted more time to fight the Baali \u00e0s they'd have more reason to and wouldn't be wasting efforts with the Salubri.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T00:57:16-07:00","id":1561648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561612-vtm-mtas-crossover-if-tremere-didn\u2019t-choose-vampirism?p=1561626#post1561626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We do know his personality, and it suggests no infernalism. He, Goratrix, and the rest of House Tremere didn't like diabolism for a simple reason - if a demon is powerful enough to be worth summoning, it can't be controlled, and if it can be controlled, it isn't powerful enough to be worth it. He'd probably pursue lichdom or another Spell of Life variant.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's stated that one of the reasons he rejected infernalism is because he'd already tried it and then came to that realisation. So, I don't think he'd do it again, but he has done it in the past (as has Etrius, and possibly Goratrix, given he was rescued from the pyre by Tremere).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> His remaining loyal to the Order of Hermes means not only that they don't have to deal with Grimgoth's betrayal, but also that they don't have to split resources between fighting the OoR and the Tremere, and that the Hermetics largely remain ignorant of the Camarilla, and likely don't have as big of a grudge against vampires. He or one of his House might eventually rise to political power within the Council of Nine, possibly even taking the role of Porthos in the main timeline. The OoR also might not win Mistridge, or at least have a much harder fight. If the OoR doesn't get Mistridge, then the Law of Shade likely doesn't exist, and Tradition magi operate openly, resulting in a radically different Consensus.<br /> <br /> As for the vampire history, the Banu Haqim don't get hit with the Tremere curse and continue being diablerists. This means that the Via Sanguinis mostly stays in its traditional form. This also means that when Ur-Shulgi wakes up, he doesn't have as much leverage, and in fact, may himself be on the menu.<br /> <br /> There are two realistic possibilities here - either the Banu Haqim join the Camarilla to fill the void in the timeline left by the Tremere, or the Sabbat fights the Camarilla on more equal ground as Koldunic sorcerers and Abyssal mystics beat them back (as Heavy Arms said). But then again, the Sabbat also loses troops; for example, the Salubri Warriors never join the Sabbat, since they're mostly there because the majority of Tremere are in the Camarilla. In fact, the Salubri in general are spared from the purges, and Saulot either never gets diablerized, or has to find another blood sorcerer to carry out his grand plan (possibly Ur-Shulgi). The Salubri likely become one of the pillars of the Camarilla, and make the Camarilla altogether a morally better group. </div> </div> </div>It's possible the Setites might end up joining the Camarilla instead of the Assamites. The Assamites would still be doing all their diablerie in Eastern Europe, and that's not much changed without the Tremere, but the Ivory Tower might make it a higher priority to get another clan.<br /> <br /> The Salubri are an interesting one. V20DA offers an alternative future whether the Salubri become a pillar clan of the Sabbat. Without Tremere persecution, the same pressures might not be there, but the Warriors would still seek out foes among the infernalists. Would they also see puppets of the Antediluvians as a problem? Because if Saulot wasn't martyred, it's possible his childer would learn he was a dick sooner, and many of them may opt to join the Anarch Revolt as a result.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, part of the appeal is that having the Salubri in the Sabbat makes for an even more spiritual, perhaps more stable, sect. It's a very cool idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T01:37:49-07:00","id":1561649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561612-vtm-mtas-crossover-if-tremere-didn\u2019t-choose-vampirism#post1561612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and one of his apprentice Grimgroth made the Mistbridge fall and pushed the found of Technocracy greatly)</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 23 of the Revised <i>NWO</i> book suggests that the importance of Mistridge is more symbolic for both the Traditions and OoR. I suspect you could swap it out with another similar event and little would be lost.<br /> <br /> Also, the exact identity of Grimgroth seems a bit in question. Like, there's a member of the Council of Seven with that name, and there's this historical figure with that name (though notably spelled differently in DA:M), but I can't find anything directly tying the two together beyond that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T17:43:06-07:00","id":1561667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561612-vtm-mtas-crossover-if-tremere-didn\u2019t-choose-vampirism#post1561612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I guess he would seek other immortality methods, like a variant of Lichdom</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lichdom is exactly what they do in Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Tremere gain immortality, but they need to consume the souls of Awakened Mages in order to sustain it.<br /> <br /> <br /> But the Tremere didn't just choose vampirism as their first option for becoming immortal. They already had invented life extending elixirs before that.<br /> <br /> The problem was that as the power of magic started to wane in the world, these elixirs became less and less effective, until they eventually just stopped working.<br /> <br /> Stealing immortality from vampires was meant to be a backup plan, because their usual methods were no longer reliable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T18:15:12-07:00","id":1561669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561612-vtm-mtas-crossover-if-tremere-didn\u2019t-choose-vampirism?p=1561667#post1561667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Lichdom is exactly what they do in Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Tremere gain immortality, but they need to consume the souls of Awakened Mages in order to sustain it.<br /> <br /> <br /> But the Tremere didn't just choose vampirism as their first option for becoming immortal. They already had invented life extending elixirs before that.<br /> <br /> The problem was that as the power of magic started to wane in the world, these elixirs became less and less effective, until they eventually just stopped working.<br /> <br /> Stealing immortality from vampires was meant to be a backup plan, because their usual methods were no longer reliable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Caveats:<br /> <br /> 1- The Tremere-Lich from Chronicles just use the name. They're not the Tremere of VtM in a variant timeline.<br /> <br /> 2- Their elixirs hadn't yet reached the point of not working. The Tremere started to search for alternatives as soon as they noticed the problem.<br /> <br /> 3- Is hard to say if this was the power of Magic waning, the effect was mostly on life-extending effects specifically. While the Backlash appear in this time, other Magics remained powerful and effective.<br /> <br /> 4- This was not a backup plan. It was a failed plan. Goratrix expected the concoction to give them immortality without turning them into real Vampires. The transformation was unexpected and regretted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-14T03:36:24-07:00","id":1561674,"title":"","content":"I quite like the approach of <i>House of Tremere</i>. It's not that magic is waning, it's that the Tremere's approach is waning. They got ahead by being particularly systemic and dogmatic about their magic in an organisation that already tends to encourage those traits. But that means when magic changes, they're unable to respond.<br /> <br /> Given that, I'd imagine Tremere without vampirism going the way of his alter-ego in later editions of <i>Ars Magica</i>; dying a broken man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-14T06:33:04-07:00","id":1561678,"title":"","content":"Without the Tremere, both the Camarilla and the Sabbat never form. The Tremere coming into existence with their self-embrace came at a pivotal time and really shook up the status-quo. The Tremere form in the latter half of the 1080s, and due to the nature of their turning, end up causing the Omen War through the next few centuries. So you have the Tremere on one side the the Tzimisce on the other. The Ventrue side with the Tremere because of their interest in Eastern Europe. Bam inquisition hits. This new pressure spurs on the Anarch revolt which in turn causes the &quot;Founders&quot; to begin forming the Camarilla. Yet without the Tremere there, the nasant Camarilla has no sorcery for communication and coordination, and likely never actually forms. With no Camarilla there is no Convention of Thorns, which means no Assamite curse. The Convention of Thorns is also what galvanized groups of Anarchs to form the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> By the 1500s you have a much different landscape of relationships and politics. The Ventrue, Toreador, Nosferatu, and Malkavian clans would be mostly the same. The Gangrel - Tzimisce alliances would have never happened. The Lasombra still attempt patricide but most likely the Tzimisce do not. The Cappodocian still get taken over by the Giovanni and the Salubri are still around in numbers. Most likely the system of High-Low clans stays in place as it did in the Dark Ages. If you want to have sects though I would see it like this:<br /> <br /> Sect 1: Ventrue, Toreador, Nosferatu, Malkavian, Setite, Salubri Healers. Camarilla like group.<br /> Sect 2: Brujah, Gangrel, Gratiano's Lasombra. This group would be more like modern day Anarchs<br /> Sect 3: Assamite, Lasombra, Salubri Warriors, and various &quot;Antitribu.&quot; Your Sabbat group, but more closely resembling the Ashirra.<br /> Independents: Giovanni, Tzimisce, Ravnos, Gangrel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-14T06:52:08-07:00","id":1561681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561612-vtm-mtas-crossover-if-tremere-didn\u2019t-choose-vampirism?p=1561678#post1561678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet without the Tremere there, the nasant Camarilla has no sorcery for communication and coordination, and likely never actually forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the lack of Tremere sorcery would be the bigger impact.<br /> <br /> Other forms of sorcery existed. The Tremere added magic-as-service to the menu, but didn't create magic in the first place, and the need for answering to the Inquisition is more relevant than the means of communication, that already included Animalism and Auspex when it really needed to outpace letters, which is itself not a bad option.<br /> <br /> While I agree things would change dramatically and may very well mean the sects as we know don't form I don't think the lack of magic comm would stop the formation of an alliance to fight the Inquisition by enforcing the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> The Tremere are more relevant due to how they shaped politics by making allies and enemies. And the Curse on the Banu Haqim, that totally counts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-14T22:36:25-07:00","id":1561699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561612-vtm-mtas-crossover-if-tremere-didn\u2019t-choose-vampirism?p=1561678#post1561678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet without the Tremere there, the nasant Camarilla has no sorcery for communication and coordination, and likely never actually forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Several of the clans have access to Blood Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Hell, even the Anarchs have their own version of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy is a STYLE of blood sorcery, but is not the discipline of blood sorcery itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> The problem wasn't that the Tremere were their only option. The problem came in two other major factors. First of all, was the Camarilla made certain demands the other clans found unacceptable, like telling the Followers of Set that if they wanted to join up, they'd have to abandon the use of Serpentis.<br /> <br /> The second problem, was the Tremere running a smear campaign on every other blood sorcerer they could find, in order to publicly discredit them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T01:47:03-07:00","id":1561700,"title":"","content":"I think part of the problem is that early edition Tremere were in a very different spot than they <i>should</i> have been if you would rewind current canon. Exclusivity to Blood Sorcery is only part of it, but plenty narrative band-aids were needed to preserve core canon and keep the Tremere in the Cam.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm not sure the Convention of Thorns would have gone the way it did even with the Tremere extant as vampires. I could see the case for Tremere and Giovanni to throw in with the Anarchs/Sabbat and the Followers of Set taking their place in the Camarilla. They're even more qualified for the Scheming Vizier role anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T02:42:21-07:00","id":1561702,"title":"","content":"There was no Anarchs at the time, and the Sabbat was a marginal movement with some traits the Tremere weren't very keen on adopting.<br /> <br /> I think their allegiance to the Cam makes sense as they sought to ingratiate themselves to the powerful, and definitely valued strict hierarchy. The Sabbat wouldn't suffer the Pyramid, and it was a nonnegotiable for the clan.<br /> <br /> Now, it's debatable if they'd manage this level of success. The setting as is today has plenty of things the Tremere pushed aside that should not have been so simple to dismiss. Certainly their success is a prescribed outcome: they did it because Rein-Hagen wanted the Tremere as the Magic Clan\u2122 from Ars Magica.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T03:57:05-07:00","id":1561703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561612-vtm-mtas-crossover-if-tremere-didn\u2019t-choose-vampirism?p=1561702#post1561702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was no Anarchs at the time, and the Sabbat was a marginal movement with some traits the Tremere weren't very keen on adopting.<br /> <br /> I think their allegiance to the Cam makes sense as they sought to ingratiate themselves to the powerful, and definitely valued strict hierarchy. The Sabbat wouldn't suffer the Pyramid, and it was a nonnegotiable for the clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah sorry, with Anarchs I meant the proto-Sabbat, not the modern day type. True about the incompatibilities, but the concessions could have gone both ways. IMO the Sabbat having to tolerate the Pyramid isn't as outlandish as a compromise as the Cam tolerating the open diablerie of Saulot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561612-vtm-mtas-crossover-if-tremere-didn\u2019t-choose-vampirism?p=1561702#post1561702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, it's debatable if they'd manage this level of success. The setting as is today has plenty of things the Tremere pushed aside that should not have been so simple to dismiss. Certainly their success is a prescribed outcome: they did it because Rein-Hagen wanted the Tremere as the Magic Clan\u2122 from Ars Magica.</div> </div> </div> </div>I concur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T08:40:59-07:00","id":1561712,"title":"","content":"Were I to remake the Tremere, the one thing I'd get rid of would be the destruction of the Salubri. I don't think anyone would sit well with it, as if wasn't exclusively about Elders, either.<br /> <br /> Instead, I'd have them still use the original elixir to this day, so 8th Gen Tremere would be those transformed by the old method rather than Embraced and Character Creation would have no need for changes (in lore they started 9th IIRC).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T15:32:43-07:00","id":1561741,"title":"","content":"At the risk of oversimplifying some pretty profound moments in the history of the lore, I attribute the Tremere's place in the Camrilla entirely to the German Ventrue's desire for an ally against the Tzimisce in their greed to expand eastward and the Tremere's convenient location in Ceoris. Without a Clan Tremere, what do the Ventrue do to advance their goals?<br /> <br /> Saulot would still require a patsy for his scheme to adopt a new clan by manipulating someone into diablerizing him, and Ventrue clan legend has it that their founder died outside the walls outside the second city; maybe one of the German invaders gets chosen by Saulot to do the deed, although I think the Tremere's focus on mystical research was as much a part of the reason why Saulot chose them as their desperation.<br /> <br /> I'm afraid it isn't good news for the Salubri, no matter what clan devours their founder and is devoured in turn by him. They're abandoned, and whichever clan Saulot takes over is still likely to pursue the pogrom.<br /> <br /> I imagine the Sabbat still forming, as the Tzimisce and Lasombra clans still have cultures that create the tension that leads to what happens with their founders, and without the presence of a Clan Tremere in Transylvania, both clans consider the Ventrue their biggest rivals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T16:08:27-07:00","id":1561742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561612-vtm-mtas-crossover-if-tremere-didn\u2019t-choose-vampirism?p=1561741#post1561741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of oversimplifying some pretty profound moments in the history of the lore, I attribute the Tremere's place in the Camrilla entirely to the German Ventrue's desire for an ally against the Tzimisce in their greed to expand eastward and the Tremere's convenient location in Ceoris. Without a Clan Tremere, what do the Ventrue do to advance their goals?<br /> <br /> Saulot would still require a patsy for his scheme</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to remember that the whole &quot;Saulot scheme&quot; thing is a rumor, not a canonical fact.<br /> <br /> A rumor I personally don't follow because it only exists to appease people who didn't like the Salubri and Saulot to begin with. It's very lame as it goes hugely overboard in making him the ultimate badass evil lord just to overcompensate his initial depiction of \u2013 crime of crimes \u2013 being good for a change.<br /> <br /> Grimdark WoD for me is insufferable, kills everything truly Punk or Gothic about the setting to turn it into War Hammer Modern. The Emperor himself would be disgusted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T20:43:40-07:00","id":1561751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561612-vtm-mtas-crossover-if-tremere-didn\u2019t-choose-vampirism?p=1561742#post1561742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grimdark WoD for me is insufferable, kills everything truly Punk or Gothic about the setting to turn it into War Hammer Modern. The Emperor himself would be disgusted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not every thread needs to become about how much you dislike the lore, but in this instance I'll be guilty of going along with the derail long enough to point out that the innocent Salubri's abandonment by their sire is a part of their personal horror for me, for deeply personal reasons, and that the descendants of the bloodline who survive into the modern nights are free to find their own purpose is part of their hope. I like it. It's what allows the bloodline to hook me. Your mileage may vary.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T20:58:05-07:00","id":1561753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561612-vtm-mtas-crossover-if-tremere-didn\u2019t-choose-vampirism?p=1561751#post1561751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not every thread needs to become about how much you dislike the lore</div> </div> </div> </div>My first and main point is entirely about it not being a fact in the lore, it's an open question.<br /> <br /> The diatribe about this development is merely that. An aside to externalize my frustration at no one in particular.<br /> <br /> Neither is your idea or preference being attacked, and yours is indeed an interesting view. But still not the view that birthed the trend in the lore in the first place, for whatever it's worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T07:37:18-07:00","id":1561765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561612-vtm-mtas-crossover-if-tremere-didn\u2019t-choose-vampirism?p=1561741#post1561741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Saulot would still require a patsy for his scheme to adopt a new clan by manipulating someone into diablerizing him, and Ventrue clan legend has it that their founder died outside the walls outside the second city; maybe one of the German invaders gets chosen by Saulot to do the deed, although I think the Tremere's focus on mystical research was as much a part of the reason why Saulot chose them as their desperation.<br /> <br /> I'm afraid it isn't good news for the Salubri, no matter what clan devours their founder and is devoured in turn by him. They're abandoned, and whichever clan Saulot takes over is still likely to pursue the pogrom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that it took several hundred years for Saulot to properly take control of Tremere, and that Tremere mostly did the pogrom on his own.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the Setites and Banu Haqim would be obvious targets if not Tremere. Perhaps he'd wake Ur-Shulgi and trick him into diablerizing him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T17:22:20-07:00","id":1561795,"title":"","content":"I do remember that Saulot greatly underestimated how powerful Tremere himself was &amp; saw him him as a &quot;typical&quot; ancille with average willpower and didn't know that Tremere was a master level mage with several centuries of life and had considerable willpower that would be &quot;normal&quot; for such people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T22:56:19-07:00","id":1561807,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, at least early on there was the option that Saulot may also have been Cappadocius (that is, Ashur) which would make the Giovanni a replacement if the Tremere weren't available. That seems very unlikely now, but there are some parallels in how a spiritual Clan was changed into a more secular version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T00:10:31-07:00","id":1561810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561612-vtm-mtas-crossover-if-tremere-didn\u2019t-choose-vampirism?p=1561765#post1561765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, the Setites and Banu Haqim would be obvious targets if not Tremere. Perhaps he'd wake Ur-Shulgi and trick him into diablerizing him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if engaging with this idea, I wouldn't use the other clans for this.<br /> <br /> What made the Tremere an interesting case was precisely their lack of a 3rd Generation progenitor. Not just dead, but never existed. They spawned through Magic at 9th Gen and worked from there, making them a perfect clean slate.<br /> <br /> They didn't even had a Weakness, as theirs was actually subservience to the Pyramid through blackmail.<br /> <br /> It would be hard to achieve anything taking a well established clan with long tradition and a founder. Would work as infiltration, but not really as reformation.<br /> <br /> A Bloodline would work better, preferably one new and with little relationship to the parent clan. It would even let influence the evolution of their signature Discipline more than he could really influence Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> Kyasid come to mind. Daughters of Cacophony, Blood Brothers, even alternative Gargoyles. It could be a new one crafted by others under influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T18:24:15-07:00","id":1561916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561612-vtm-mtas-crossover-if-tremere-didn\u2019t-choose-vampirism?p=1561810#post1561810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if engaging with this idea, I wouldn't use the other clans for this.<br /> <br /> What made the Tremere an interesting case was precisely their lack of a 3rd Generation progenitor. Not just dead, but never existed. They spawned through Magic at 9th Gen and worked from there, making them a perfect clean slate.<br /> <br /> They didn't even had a Weakness, as theirs was actually subservience to the Pyramid through blackmail.<br /> <br /> It would be hard to achieve anything taking a well established clan with long tradition and a founder. Would work as infiltration, but not really as reformation.<br /> <br /> A Bloodline would work better, preferably one new and with little relationship to the parent clan. It would even let influence the evolution of their signature Discipline more than he could really influence Thaumaturgy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that he was looking for a blood sorcery discipline at rating 10 so he could develop a ritual to split his Hun and P'o.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T18:39:16-07:00","id":1561919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561612-vtm-mtas-crossover-if-tremere-didn\u2019t-choose-vampirism?p=1561916#post1561916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that he was looking for a blood sorcery discipline at rating 10 so he could develop a ritual to split his Hun and P'o.</div> </div> </div> </div>He didn't need a clan for that. With all his travels and contacts, he probably already had a working basis of Dur An Ki, maybe Akhu too. It may not be easy, but taking over an entire clan through a convoluted plan involving diablerie is really too much for that.<br /> <br /> Maybe there was something specific to the Tremere half-Awakened Thaumaturgy, but then existing clans wouldn't do the trick.<br /> <br /> I think a bloodline opens more avenues to build something both from Watsonian and Doylist perspectives, and just as the Tremere this bloodline would have raised to clan status as a result of the plan (the Tremere were a bloodline and a minor one at that).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}